== Land acknowledgement ==

"We acknowledge that Thunder Bay is built on the traditional territory of the Anishinabek, which includes the Ojibwa of Fort William First Nation, signatory to the Robinson-Superior Treaty of 1850. We also acknowledge the contributions of the Métis peoples." — [https://www.thunderbay.ca/city-hall/history-heritage-and-records/history-of-thunder-bay/ City of Thunder Bay], quoted as published.

Addresses on Fort William First Nation land are a separate phase of this import. They are not uploaded until the Nation has been asked and given time to answer; see [[#Fort William First Nation|§ Fort William First Nation]].

== Summary ==

Human-reviewed import of '''missing civic address points''' from the City of Thunder Bay's municipal address layer. Each address is checked against a fresh OSM snapshot, so only addresses OSM does not already have are created. Every run is reviewed by a person in a local web UI before it is uploaded. Every upload is its own tagged changeset, and every decision is logged.

Thunder Bay today has almost no per-address data in OSM beyond loose CanVec nodes. A 2026-08-16 sample of the city found 985 of 1,006 address-bearing elements to be CanVec 6.0 nodes, quiet since a 2018 retag, with no import tags, no import page and no recent address activity.

'''Geographic scope:''' the City of Thunder Bay, Ontario, plus Fort William First Nation land in a separate phase. The City's 7 wards (Westfort, McIntyre, Neebing, Red River, Northwood, McKellar, Current River) split the work into review tiles.

