== Goals and non-goals ==

=== Goals ===
* Add the civic addresses OSM is missing in Thunder Bay, from the City's authoritative roster.
* Create no duplicates of addresses already in OSM, and change no existing address data.
* Keep a per-address audit trail (source row → verdict → reviewer decision → changeset → OSM id) anyone can inspect.

=== Non-goals ===
* '''No deletions''', '''no edits to existing objects''', '''no geometry edits''', '''no buildings''' and '''no <code>addr:interpolation</code> cleanup'''. Create-only, exactly as [[Toronto/Import/AddressPoints#Goals and non-goals|Toronto's]].
* '''Not the existing CanVec nodes.''' Where a CanVec node already carries the address, it counts as a match and nothing is uploaded. Retiring or merging CanVec nodes would be a separate proposal.

== Schedule ==

=== Contacts and reviewers ===
* '''Maintainer and first reviewer:''' toronto@comentality.com
* '''Local mappers contacted before this page went up:''' Matthew Darwin, eireidium. Both are invited to review.
* '''Fort William First Nation:''' Lands & Governance, by letter on {{TBD: date sent}}. See [[#Fort William First Nation|below]].
* '''Upload rule:''' nothing uploads without a reviewer's approval in the web UI.

=== Phases ===

Each phase can ship on its own and be reverted on its own.

* '''Phase 0 — community review.''' This page, a forum post tagged <code>import</code>, and a 14-day feedback window.
* '''Phase 1 — pilot, one tile.''' {{TBD: tile name}}, {{TBD: n}} candidates, fully reviewed by hand. One-week hold before Phase 2.
* '''Phase 2 — the City, ward by ward.''' One tile per changeset, 250–750 source addresses each, at most one changeset a minute by manual cadence.
* '''Phase 3 — Fort William First Nation.''' Only after the Nation has answered, or after the wait in [[#Fort William First Nation|§ Fort William First Nation]]. Its own tiles and changesets, never mixed with City tiles.
* '''Phase 4 — closeout and upkeep.''' A closing report here and on the forum thread. After that the City's new addresses are added monthly under the same rules, as for [[Toronto/Import/AddressPoints#Continuous maintenance|Toronto]].

== Fort William First Nation ==

The City's address layer includes 378 points on Fort William First Nation land, a separate jurisdiction from the City. They have no City parcel number. The City publishes them under the same open licence, so the licence permits importing them. We are asking the Nation anyway, because adding a community's addresses without asking is not how we want to work. There is no Canadian OSM import precedent we could find either way.

* A letter went to FWFN Lands & Governance on {{TBD}} asking: whether the Nation is comfortable with the addresses being in OSM; who assigns them; what the road the City lists as "Squaw Bay Road" is called today; and whether there is a process to follow.
* '''If the Nation says no''', Phase 3 does not happen, and this page says so.
* '''If the Nation asks for changes''' (names, spellings, a subset), we make them.
* '''If there is no reply''' after {{TBD: wait — operator's decision}} days and a phone follow-up, {{TBD: what then}}.
* '''84 addresses on "Squaw Bay Road"''' will not be uploaded under that name in any case. The word is a slur, and Canada has been renaming places that carry it. We will use the name the Nation gives.
* '''8 points have no civic number''' and are dropped.

== Import data ==

=== Source ===
* '''Dataset:''' Municipal Address layer, City of Thunder Bay ([https://services5.arcgis.com/h9xShea49ZANgOtx/arcgis/rest/services/Municipal_Address_Feature_Layer/FeatureServer/0 ArcGIS feature service]).
* '''Consumption path:''' fetched daily into a SQLite history by [https://github.com/skfd/ontario-address-changes ontario-address-changes] ([https://skfd.github.io/ontario-address-changes/thunder-bay/ change reports]); this import reads that read-only.

=== Licence ===
* '''Licence:''' City of Thunder Bay Open Data Licence, listed as OSM-compatible {{TBD: link to the LWG/wiki listing}}. Attribution goes in <code>addr:source</code> on each node and <code>source</code> on each changeset.

=== Type and volume ===
* Points only: civic number, street, municipality (<code>THUNDER BAY</code> or <code>FWFN</code>), parcel id, property type. No units, no postcodes, no ranges.

=== Freshness ===
* OSM side: Geofabrik Ontario extract, refreshed before each session. If more than 24 h pass between conflation and upload, re-conflate first.

== Tagging plan ==

All uploads are '''nodes'''.

{| class="wikitable"
! Tag !! From !! Notes
|-
| <code>addr:housenumber</code> || <code>ADDRESS</code> || The full civic number with its qualifier: <code>688B</code>, <code>963 1/2</code>. The City's integer column drops qualifiers on 338 rows, so it is not used.
|-
| <code>addr:street</code> || <code>ROOT</code> || The City publishes abbreviated capitals (<code>JAMES ST S</code>); expanded and title-cased on the way out: <code>James Street South</code>, <code>103rd Street</code>.
|-
| <code>addr:source</code> || static || <code>City of Thunder Bay Open Data</code>
|-
| <code>addr:postcode</code> || OSM || Only copied from a same-address POI already in OSM. The City publishes no postcodes, and none are invented.
|}

'''Not written:''' <code>addr:city</code> (redundant inside the city; for FWFN, ask the Nation first), <code>addr:province</code>, <code>addr:country</code>, <code>addr:unit</code> (no unit field), ward, parcel id, property type.

